Create guidelines, principles and phases for best practices

Phases: 

    - Phase 1: Product Discovery & Scoping:
        Tools: Jira / Confluence, Free Tier.
        
        Brand & Content Audit: 
            Analyze the target site (e.g., Cayman Rugby). 
            Identify pain points, key user roles (guest, club member, admin), and core functionality.
        User Stories & Acceptance Criteria: 
            Write user stories in Jira using standard formats (e.g., "As a member, I want to view upcoming fixtures so that I can RSVP"). 
            Define explicit Acceptance Criteria (AC).
        Sprint Planning: 
            Break down the project into 2-week epics (e.g., Authentication, Fixture Management, Admin Dashboard).
    
    - Phase 2: UI/UX & Visual Design:
        Tools: Figma
        
        Wireframing: Create low-fidelity wireframes focusing on layout, content hierarchy, and navigation structure.
        Design System & Tokens: Define color palettes, typography scales, spacing tokens, and UI components (buttons, input fields, cards).
        High-Fidelity Mockups & Interactive Prototypes: Design pixel-perfect desktop and mobile views with interactive flows for testing user journeys.
    
    - Phase 3: Architecture & System Design:
        Tools: Mermaid.js, Excalidraw, DBDiagram.io
        
        Data Modeling: Map out relational or non-relational schemas with explicit foreign keys, indices, and constraints.
        API Contract Design: Define RESTful endpoints or GraphQL schemas, request/response payloads, HTTP status codes, and error formats.
        System Diagram: Diagram the data flow between client, API gateway/server, auth service, database, and mock third-party services (e.g., mock payment gateway).
    
    - Phase 4: Repository & Environment Setup:
        Tools: GitHub, Docker
        
        Monorepo / Workspace Setup: 
            Initialize a clean folder structure (e.g., /apps/web, /apps/api, /packages/config).
        CI/CD & Linter Configuration: 
            Set up ESLint, Prettier, Husky pre-commit hooks, and GitHub Actions workflows for automated linting and type-checking.
        Mock Data Strategy: 
            Seed scripts using libraries like @faker-js/faker to populate relational databases with realistic domain data.
    
    - Phase 5: Core Implementation:
        Frontend, Backend, Database
        
        Backend First (or Parallel): 
            Implement API endpoints, database ORM models/migrations, and authentication pipelines (JWT / Session).
        Frontend Implementation: 
            Build reusable components based on Figma design tokens, integrating state management and API clients with type safety.
    
    - Phase 6: Quality Assurance & Testing:
        Tools: Jest, Vitest, Playwright/Cypress
        
        Unit Tests: Test isolated utilities, business logic, and component state transitions.
        Integration Tests: Validate API endpoints against a test database environment (request -> response -> database side-effects).
        End-to-End (E2E) Tests: Automate critical user journeys in a real browser context (e.g., full checkout or RSVP flow).
    
    - Phase 7: Showcase & Documentation:
        Tools: Loom / OBS, GitHub Markdown
        
        Comprehensive README: Document architecture, setup instructions, ERDs, and design rationale.
        Video Walkthrough: Record a 3–5 minute video demonstrating product feature flows, code architecture highlights, and Figma-to-code alignment.

